---
import ApplicationLayout from '../../layouts/ApplicationLayout.astro';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Product",
    "name": "DMB-028 Manual-Clean Centrifuge Module - Alfa Laval MAB 206",
    "description": "The Dolphin DMB-028 is a turnkey manual-clean purification module featuring a remanufactured Alfa Laval MAB 206 disc stack centrifuge, rebuilt, tested, and warrantied by Dolphin. Published diesel capacity at 40°C and 13 cSt is 6,400 L/h (28.18 US GPM, derived), with a 7.5 HP motor. High-capacity module for large turbine lube oil systems and industrial fluid purification.",
    "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": "Alfa Laval" },
    "alternateName": "Alfa Laval MAB 206",
    "category": "Disc Stack Centrifuges",
    "model": "DMB-028",
    "offers": {
      "@type": "Offer",
      "availability": "https://schema.org/InStock",
      "priceCurrency": "USD",
      "seller": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Dolphin Centrifuge" }
    }
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "DMB-028 Manual-Clean Centrifuge Module (Alfa Laval MAB 206) - Specifications & Applications",
    "author": {
      "@type": "Person",
      "name": "Sanjay Prabhu MSME",
      "jobTitle": "Centrifuge Applications Engineer",
      "worksFor": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Dolphin Centrifuge" }
    },
    "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Dolphin Centrifuge" },
    "url": "https://dolphincentrifuge.com/centrifuges/dmb-028/"
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is the throughput of the DMB-028 centrifuge?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Published MAB 206 capacities are 6,400 L/h diesel fuel at 40°C and 13 cSt (28.18 US GPM, derived), 8,500 L/h gas oil at 40°C (37.42 US GPM, derived), 2,900–3,300 L/h R&O lube oil at 80–90°C (12.77–14.53 US GPM, derived), and 6,200 L/h steam turbine oil at 60–70°C (27.30 US GPM, derived). The rated reference is 9,500 L/h (41.83 US GPM, derived); its source fluid is unspecified. The base machine uses a 7.5 HP motor."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What turbine or industrial application is the DMB-028 sized for?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "At the published R&O lube-oil range of 2,900–3,300 L/h at 80–90°C (12.77–14.53 US GPM, derived), the DMB-028 is suited for large turbine generators in the 10,000–25,000 HP range, large industrial gearboxes, or multiple smaller turbines sharing a centralized lube oil purification system. It is also commonly used for large diesel fuel polishing systems and high-throughput gas oil clarification."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "When should I choose the DMB-028 over the DMPX-028 self-cleaning model?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The DMB-028 base machine has a published diesel capacity at 40°C and 13 cSt of 6,400 L/h (28.18 US GPM, derived). The DMPX-028 is a self-cleaning commercial class with more than one Alfa Laval base machine, so its capacity must be stated for the exact base machine and fluid. Choose manual-clean for low-solids feeds with manageable cleaning shutdowns and self-cleaning for significant solids or continuous unattended operation."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How does the DMB-028 compare to the DMB-019 and DMB-037?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "At the same published diesel condition of 40°C and 13 cSt, the DMB-028 base machine is rated at 6,400 L/h (28.18 US GPM, derived), between the DMB-019 at 4,400 L/h (19.37 US GPM, derived) and DMB-037 at 8,400 L/h (36.98 US GPM, derived). Its published R&O range at 80–90°C is 2,900–3,300 L/h (12.77–14.53 US GPM, derived); the DMB-037 range under the same conditions is 3,800–4,400 L/h (16.73–19.37 US GPM, derived)."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Can the DMB-028 serve a centralized lube oil system for multiple machines?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Yes. The published MAB 206 R&O capacity at 80–90°C is 2,900–3,300 L/h (12.77–14.53 US GPM, derived), and its diesel capacity at 40°C and 13 cSt is 6,400 L/h (28.18 US GPM, derived). The DMB-028 is well suited for centralized lube oil systems serving multiple industrial machines from a common reservoir. Contact Dolphin Centrifuge to size the system for your specific configuration."
        }
      }
    ]
  }
];
---

<ApplicationLayout
  title="DMB-028 Manual-Clean Module - Alfa Laval MAB 206 | Dolphin Centrifuge"
  heroTitle="DMB-028 Manual-Clean Module - Alfa Laval MAB 206"
  disableTitleSuffix={true}
  description="Dolphin DMB-028 module with a remanufactured Alfa Laval MAB 206: published diesel capacity at 40°C and 13 cSt is 6,400 L/h (28.18 US GPM, derived), with a 7.5 HP motor."
  canonicalUrl="https://dolphincentrifuge.com/centrifuges/dmb-028/"
  heroImage="/images/alfa-laval-mab-centrifuge/alfa-laval-mab-206-lube-oil-module-hero-1800.webp"
  heroImageAlt="Remanufactured Alfa Laval MAB 206 centrifuge module with Dolphin control panel, supplied as the DMB-028 system"
  category="products"
  categoryLabel="Dolphin Manual-Clean Disc Centrifuges"
  toc={[
    { id: "specs", label: "Specifications" },
    { id: "capacity", label: "Capacity by Application" },
    { id: "applications", label: "Key Applications" },
    { id: "faq", label: "FAQ" },
  ]}
  relatedApplications={[
    { label: "Lube Oil Centrifuge", href: "/lube-oil-centrifuge/" },
    { label: "Fuel Oil Centrifuge", href: "/fuel-oil-centrifuge/" },
    { label: "Waste Oil Centrifuge", href: "/waste-oil-centrifuge/" },
  ]}
  relatedProducts={[
    { label: "DMB-019 Manual-Clean Centrifuge", href: "/centrifuges/dmb-019/" },
    { label: "DMB-037 Manual-Clean Centrifuge", href: "/centrifuges/dmb-037/" },
    { label: "DMPX-028 Self-Cleaning Centrifuge", href: "/centrifuges/dmpx-028/" },
  ]}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  hideBottomCTA={true}
>
  <article class="prose-dolphin max-w-none">

    <p>The DMB-028 is a Dolphin-engineered turnkey purification module featuring a remanufactured <a href="/alfa-laval-mab-centrifuge/">Alfa Laval MAB 206</a> manual-clean disc stack centrifuge, rebuilt, tested, and warrantied by Dolphin.</p>
    <p>Dolphin is the independent specialist in Alfa Laval centrifuges, with 40+ years of hands-on MAB experience behind every module we ship.</p>

    <h2 id="specs">DMB-028 Specifications</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Parameter</th>
            <th>Value</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Base machine</td><td>Alfa Laval MAB 206 (remanufactured)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Separation type</td><td>Two-phase clarifier (liquid-liquid or liquid-solid)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Diesel throughput at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt</td><td>6,400 L/h (28.18 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Rated reference (source fluid unspecified)</td><td>9,500 L/h (41.83 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bowl speed</td><td>~8,700 RPM</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Drive motor</td><td>7.5 HP</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Cleaning method</td><td>Manual (bowl disassembly required for solids removal)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bowl construction</td><td>Carbon steel standard</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Power supply</td><td>460V / 3-phase / 60 Hz standard (other voltages available)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 italic">Throughput figures are for typical fluids at listed conditions. Actual capacity varies with feed viscosity, temperature, density difference, and solids loading.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 italic">Dolphin is an independent remanufacturer and is not affiliated with Alfa Laval.</p>

    <div class="bg-gold/10 border-l-4 border-gold rounded-r-xl p-5 my-8 not-prose">
      <p class="font-bold text-navy text-base mb-1">Need the complete datasheet?</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-light leading-relaxed mb-4">We'll email the complete datasheet - usually within one business day.</p>
      <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/" class="inline-block bg-gold text-navy font-semibold px-5 py-2 rounded-lg hover:bg-gold/90 transition-colors text-sm">Request the full spec sheet (PDF) -></a>
    </div>

    <h2 id="capacity">DMB-028 Capacity by Application</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Application / Fluid</th>
            <th>Published throughput (L/h and derived US GPM)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Rated reference (source fluid unspecified)</td><td>9,500 L/h (41.83 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Gas oil at 40&deg;C</td><td>8,500 L/h (37.42 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Diesel fuel at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt</td><td>6,400 L/h (28.18 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>R&amp;O lube oil at 80&ndash;90&deg;C</td><td>2,900&ndash;3,300 L/h (12.77&ndash;14.53 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Detergent lube oil at 80&ndash;90&deg;C</td><td>2,400&ndash;2,900 L/h (10.57&ndash;12.77 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Trunk-piston detergent lube oil at 80&ndash;90&deg;C</td><td>1,700&ndash;2,100 L/h (7.48&ndash;9.25 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Engine lubricating oil at 80&ndash;90&deg;C</td><td>3,300 L/h (14.53 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Steam turbine oil at 60&ndash;70&deg;C</td><td>6,200 L/h (27.30 US GPM, derived)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 italic">US GPM values are derived from the published L/h figures using 1 US GPM = 227.124707 L/h and rounded to two decimal places. See the <a href="/technical-data/#methodology">authoritative technical-data registry and methodology</a> for source basis and machine-readable records.</p>

    <!-- Mid-Page CTA -->
    <div class="not-prose my-10 rounded-xl border-l-4 border-gold bg-gold/10 p-6 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center gap-4">
      <div class="flex-1">
        <p class="text-navy font-bold text-lg mb-1">Sizing a DMB-028 for your turbine or industrial system?</p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm">Our team calculates turnover rates, cleaning intervals, and throughput from your HP rating and reservoir volume - at no charge.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/" class="shrink-0 inline-block bg-gold text-navy font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-gold/90 transition-colors text-center">
        Request a Quote &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2 id="applications">Key Applications</h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-10 not-prose">
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-200">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-navy mb-2">Large Turbine Lube Oil Purification</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Steam and gas turbine generators in the 10,000–25,000 HP range, and large industrial turbine-driven equipment. Published MAB 206 throughput on R&amp;O lube oil at 80–90&deg;C is 2,900–3,300 L/h (12.77–14.53 US GPM, derived).</p>
        <a href="/lube-oil-centrifuge/" class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy hover:text-gold transition-colors">Lube Oil Centrifuge Details &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-200">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-navy mb-2">High-Volume Diesel &amp; Gas Oil Polishing</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Large fuel storage depots, refinery off-spec handling, and large generator installations with high daily fuel throughput. Published capacity is 6,400 L/h (28.18 US GPM, derived) on diesel at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt and 8,500 L/h (37.42 US GPM, derived) on gas oil at 40&deg;C.</p>
        <a href="/diesel-centrifuge/" class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy hover:text-gold transition-colors">Diesel Centrifuge Details &rarr;</a>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-200">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-navy mb-2">Industrial Compressor Lube Oil</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Large reciprocating compressors, centrifugal compressors, and compressor stations in gas processing and petrochemical facilities. The DMB-028 maintains lube oil cleanliness for compressors with large oil reservoir volumes where continuous high-throughput purification is needed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-200">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-navy mb-2">Central Lube Oil Systems</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Centralized lube oil systems serving multiple pieces of industrial machinery from a common reservoir. The DMB-028&rsquo;s high throughput makes it effective for large central systems where individual machine purifiers would be impractical.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">What is the throughput of the DMB-028?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Published MAB 206 capacities are 6,400 L/h diesel at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt (28.18 US GPM, derived), 8,500 L/h gas oil at 40&deg;C (37.42 US GPM, derived), 2,900&ndash;3,300 L/h R&amp;O lube oil at 80&ndash;90&deg;C (12.77&ndash;14.53 US GPM, derived), and 6,200 L/h steam turbine oil at 60&ndash;70&deg;C (27.30 US GPM, derived). The 9,500 L/h (41.83 US GPM, derived) rated reference has no source fluid specified. The base machine uses a 7.5 HP motor.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">What turbine or industrial application is the DMB-028 sized for?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        At the published R&amp;O range of 2,900&ndash;3,300 L/h at 80&ndash;90&deg;C (12.77&ndash;14.53 US GPM, derived), the DMB-028 suits large turbines in the 10,000–25,000 HP range, large industrial gearboxes, or centralized <a href="/lube-oil-centrifuge/">lube oil</a> purification for multiple machines. Its published diesel capacity at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt is 6,400 L/h (28.18 US GPM, derived).
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">When should I choose DMB-028 over the DMPX-028?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        The DMB-028 base machine has a published diesel capacity at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt of 6,400 L/h (28.18 US GPM, derived). The <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-028/">DMPX-028</a> is a self-cleaning commercial class with more than one Alfa Laval base machine, so its capacity must be stated for the exact base machine and fluid. Choose self-cleaning for significant solids or continuous unattended operation.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">How does the DMB-028 compare to the DMB-019 and DMB-037?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        At the same published diesel condition of 40&deg;C and 13 cSt, the DMB-028 base machine is rated at 6,400 L/h (28.18 US GPM, derived), between the <a href="/centrifuges/dmb-019/">DMB-019</a> at 4,400 L/h (19.37 US GPM, derived) and the <a href="/centrifuges/dmb-037/">DMB-037</a> at 8,400 L/h (36.98 US GPM, derived). Its R&amp;O range at 80&ndash;90&deg;C is 2,900&ndash;3,300 L/h (12.77&ndash;14.53 US GPM, derived). See all models at the <a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge/">disc stack centrifuge overview</a>.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details class="border-l-4 border-gold/40 pl-4 mb-4 not-prose">
      <summary class="font-semibold text-navy cursor-pointer py-2">Can the DMB-028 serve a centralized lube oil system?</summary>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Yes. The published MAB 206 R&amp;O capacity at 80&ndash;90&deg;C is 2,900&ndash;3,300 L/h (12.77&ndash;14.53 US GPM, derived). The DMB-028 is well suited for centralized systems serving multiple industrial machines from a common reservoir. <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/">Contact Dolphin Centrifuge</a> to size the system for your specific configuration and determine the optimal cleaning schedule.
      </p>
    </details>

    <h2>Related Resources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/centrifuges/dmb-019/">DMB-019 Manual-Clean Centrifuge</a></li>
      <li><a href="/centrifuges/dmb-037/">DMB-037 Manual-Clean Centrifuge</a></li>
      <li><a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-028/">DMPX-028 Self-Cleaning Centrifuge</a></li>
      <li><a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge/">Disc Stack Centrifuge Overview</a></li>
      <li><a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/">Contact Us for DMB-028 Pricing</a></li>
    </ul>

  </article>

  <!-- Bottom CTA Bar -->
  <div class="not-prose mt-12 rounded-xl bg-navy px-8 py-8 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center gap-6">
    <div class="flex-1">
      <p class="text-white font-bold text-xl mb-1">Ready to order the DMB-028?</p>
      <p class="text-white/80 text-sm">Call <a href="tel:+12485222573" class="text-gold font-semibold">(248) 522-2573</a> or email <a href="mailto:sales@dolphincentrifuge.com" class="text-gold font-semibold">sales@dolphincentrifuge.com</a> - 40+ years in centrifugal separation, Warren MI.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 shrink-0">
      <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/" class="inline-block bg-gold text-navy font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-gold/90 transition-colors text-center">Get a Quote</a>
      <a href="/industrial-centrifuge-sample-testing/" class="inline-block border border-white text-white font-bold px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-white/10 transition-colors text-center">Sample Testing</a>
    </div>
  </div>

</ApplicationLayout>
